<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oslo Accords</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1993">1993</a>–<a href="/years/1995">1995</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a> Accords were the agreements of 1993 and 1995 between Israel and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> Liberation Organization, negotiated secretly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a>, in which each side recognised the other for the first time. They created a Palestinian Authority with limited self-government in parts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bank">West Bank</a> and Gaza as a step towards a final settlement within five years. The settlement never came, and the accords' interim arrangements have endured for decades as the framework of an unfinished peace.</p></div>
